+[26] &quot;Slc40a1&quot;       &quot;Msc&quot;           &quot;Atxn1l&quot;        &quot;Mettl15&quot;       &quot;Kbtbd3&quot;       
+[1] &quot;&quot;
+[1] &quot;&quot;</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-output-end -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuc3VidGlzcyA8LSBQcm9qZWN0UENBKG9iamVjdCA9IHN1YnRpc3MsIGRvLnByaW50ID0gRkFMU0UpXG5gYGAifQ== -->
+<pre class="r"><code>subtiss &lt;- ProjectPCA(object = subtiss, do.print = FALSE)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin  -->
+<pre class="r"><code># If this fails for your subset, it may be that cells.use is more cells than you have left! Try reducing it.
+PCHeatmap(object = subtiss, pc.use = 1:3, cells.use = 70, do.balanced = TRUE, label.columns = FALSE, num.genes = 12)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-plot-begin eyJjb25kaXRpb25zIjpbXSwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo0MTQuNzA5NSwic2l6ZV9iZWhhdmlvciI6MCwid2lkdGgiOjY3MX0= -->
+<p><img src="data:image/png;base64," /></p>
+<!-- rnb-plot-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>Later on (in FindClusters and TSNE) you will pick a number of principal components to use. This has the effect of keeping the major directions of variation in the data and, ideally, supressing noise. There is no correct answer to the number to use, but a decent rule of thumb is to go until the plot plateaus.</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuUENFbGJvd1Bsb3Qob2JqZWN0ID0gc3VidGlzcylcbmBgYCJ9 -->
+<pre class="r"><code>PCElbowPlot(object = subtiss)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-plot-begin eyJjb25kaXRpb25zIjpbXSwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo0MTQuNzA5NSwic2l6ZV9iZWhhdmlvciI6MCwid2lkdGgiOjY3MX0= -->
+<p><img src="data:image/png;base64," /></p>
+<!-- rnb-plot-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>Choose the number of principal components to use.</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuIyBTZXQgbnVtYmVyIG9mIHByaW5jaXBhbCBjb21wb25lbnRzLiBcbnN1Yi5uLnBjcyA9IDVcbmBgYCJ9 -->
+<pre class="r"><code># Set number of principal components. 
+sub.n.pcs = 5</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>The clustering is performed based on a nearest neighbors graph. Cells that have similar expression will be joined together. The Louvain algorithm looks for groups of cells with high modularity–more connections within the group than between groups. The resolution parameter determines the scale…higher resolution will give more clusters, lower resolution will give fewer.</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuIyBTZXQgcmVzb2x1dGlvbiBcbnN1Yi5yZXMudXNlZCA8LSAxXG5zdWJ0aXNzIDwtIEZpbmRDbHVzdGVycyhvYmplY3QgPSBzdWJ0aXNzLCByZWR1Y3Rpb24udHlwZSA9IFwicGNhXCIsIGRpbXMudXNlID0gMTpzdWIubi5wY3MsIFxuICAgIHJlc29sdXRpb24gPSBzdWIucmVzLnVzZWQsICxwcmludC5vdXRwdXQgPSAwLCBzYXZlLlNOTiA9IFRSVUUpXG5gYGAifQ== -->
+<pre class="r"><code># Set resolution 
+sub.res.used &lt;- 1
+subtiss &lt;- FindClusters(object = subtiss, reduction.type = &quot;pca&quot;, dims.use = 1:sub.n.pcs, 
+    resolution = sub.res.used, ,print.output = 0, save.SNN = TRUE)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>To visualize</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin  -->
+<pre class="r"><code># If cells are too spread out, you can raise the perplexity. If you have few cells, try a lower perplexity (but never less than 10).
+subtiss &lt;- RunTSNE(object = subtiss, dims.use = 1:sub.n.pcs, seed.use = 10, perplexity=20)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuIyBub3RlIHRoYXQgeW91IGNhbiBzZXQgZG8ubGFiZWw9VCB0byBoZWxwIGxhYmVsIGluZGl2aWR1YWwgY2x1c3RlcnNcblRTTkVQbG90KG9iamVjdCA9IHN1YnRpc3MsIGRvLmxhYmVsID0gVClcbmBgYCJ9 -->
+<pre class="r"><code># note that you can set do.label=T to help label individual clusters
+TSNEPlot(object = subtiss, do.label = T)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-plot-begin eyJjb25kaXRpb25zIjpbXSwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo0MTQuNzA5NSwic2l6ZV9iZWhhdmlvciI6MCwid2lkdGgiOjY3MX0= -->
+<p><img src="data:image/png;base64," /></p>
+<!-- rnb-plot-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuc3VidGlzcy5tYXJrZXJzIDwtIEZpbmRBbGxNYXJrZXJzKG9iamVjdCA9IHN1YnRpc3MsIG9ubHkucG9zID0gVFJVRSwgbWluLnBjdCA9IDAuMjUsIHRocmVzaC51c2UgPSAwLjI1KVxuYGBgIn0= -->
+<pre class="r"><code>subtiss.markers &lt;- FindAllMarkers(object = subtiss, only.pos = TRUE, min.pct = 0.25, thresh.use = 0.25)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
