+<div id="assigning-subcell_ontology_classs" class="section level3">
+<h3>Assigning subcell_ontology_classs</h3>
+<p>For the subsets, we produce subcell_ontology_classs. These will be written back as metadata in the original object, so we can see all subcell_ontology_classs together.</p>
+<p>If some of the clusters you find in the subset deserve additional cell_ontology_class, you can add that right here. Use NA for clusters for which no subcell_ontology_class is needed.</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin  -->
+<pre class="r"><code>subcluster.ids &lt;- c(0, 1, 2, 3)
+subfree_annotation &lt;- c()
+subcell_ontology_class &lt;-c(&quot;Myofibroblast&quot;,&quot;Myofibroblast&quot;,&quot;Myofibroblast&quot;,&quot;Smooth_Muscle_Cells&quot;)
+subtiss@meta.data[,'subcell_ontology_class'] &lt;- plyr::mapvalues(x = subtiss@ident, from = subcluster.ids, to = subcell_ontology_class)
+tiss@meta.data[subtiss@cell.names,'subcell_ontology_class'] &lt;- as.character(subtiss@meta.data$subcell_ontology_class)
+TSNEPlot(object = subtiss, do.label = TRUE, pt.size = 0.5, group.by='subcell_ontology_class')</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-plot-begin eyJjb25kaXRpb25zIjpbXSwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo0MTQuNzA5NSwic2l6ZV9iZWhhdmlvciI6MCwid2lkdGgiOjY3MX0= -->
